A||N||6||WhiteFieroBlur||Just Got new brake light mask and GT bubls||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||11-15-2001||02:28 PM||||I ordered the Rodney third brake light mask and his Bulbs that light up the pontiac words. He says the mask is not for street but I am gonna use it for street. Do you think I would have any problems with this or does he just say that to cover anything that might come back to him. <P>Also half my words only light up and his bulbs are way brighter than stock and say get hotter but its still safe. has anyone had any problems with using them?<p>[This message has been edited by WhiteFieroBlur (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-15-2001||02:38 PM||||You more-than-likely won't ever get pulled over for having a mask on your 3rd brakelight.  Hey- I have mine disabled at the moment!  If they ever pull you over and they're looking for a bigger ticket- that's when you could get nailed for the mask.<P>As to the pontiac lights... Rodney's bulbs should be fine- although I've seen a few warped inserts, nothing drastic.  Acutally when I took my taillights apart for the clear-conversion, the far left Pontiac Bulb was burned out and the socket was partially melted.  So I just yanked out the old bulb, scraped some of the melted plastic out of the socket- and put in the new bulb.  No problems since.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WhiteFieroBlur||11-15-2001||02:52 PM||||Thanx for the info Minn, your my fastback tailight mentor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>wow just noticed I hardly have any posts and I have been on this forum for a while. I guess I need to start posting more stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||11-15-2001||02:53 PM||||I made one that says "WHOA!" for mine.  I've had police follow me and even right behind me at stoplights and never been bothered.<P>If I ever get pulled over because of it, I'll make sure the officer knows that my Fiero is an '84 so it didn't even come with a third brake light from the factory.  So there... Ha, have a nice day.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Sir, please step out of the car...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> Doh!<P>I think what Rodney is saying, you're on your own if it gets you in trouble.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||LoW_KeY||11-15-2001||03:19 PM||||I think you'll get by with it.. I've had mine in there for awhile, and the brake light didn't work GRR! <P>So I had my dads friend check it I was stumped something with the wiring near the brake pedal.  All fixed now and the police don't say nothing around my city and let me tell you I can assure you that where I live the police will get you for anything they can! <P>long as were on this subject.. I'm curious is it possible to put brighter parking lights/brake lights in with out warping the plastic? I see those newer cars with their parking lights and they sure are pretty  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000005||WhiteFieroBlur||11-15-2001||03:47 PM||||I have been looking at those plasma green back up tail lights on ebay. Anyone install a pair of these? I am surprised no one has mentioned them yet. I also am curious about the blue headlights on ebay. they are way too cheap and you know what they say, if its too good to be true..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||11-15-2001||04:14 PM||||WhiteFieroBlur...thanks for the compliment   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Don't waste your cash on their "Plasma Green" Lights- they're junk.  I picked up a pair of PIAA HyperWhite (BlueGlass) bulbs for the backups in my Clear Taillights.  They were $20/pair at <A HREF="http://www.xtremewhite.com/ORD-Light~bulbs-PIAA-Signal,Corner,Tail~and~accessories~bulbs-No-3738-1-1-1-1.cfm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xtremewhite.com/ORD-Light~bulbs-PIAA-Signal,Corner,Tail ~and~accessories~bulbs-No-3738-1-1-1-1.cfm</A>   (that's the actual item listing for them too).  I'm sure you could find something else similiar- just don't waste your money on their "plasma green"  you can get the 1156 bulbs in any color at the above link or at <A HREF="http://lightlens.com/coloredbulbs.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://lightlens.com/coloredbulbs.htm</A> <P>As to the headlight kit. I think it's worth it.  I bought mine from the Fiero Store when they first released them.  It's actually an H4 bulb conversion... which means that the bulb itself is removable without replacing the entire lens.  And you can get a huge selection of "Blue/Hyperwhite" bulbs for the H4 just about anywhere (ranging from $9-$100 depending on mfgr).  It's not "TRUE" HID, but it'd run you at least $600-700 for one of those kits.<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
